{"nodes": [{"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultralight_reviewer_ultralight", "label": "reviewer-ultralight", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultralight.md", "source_location": "frontmatter name: reviewer-ultralight (model sonnet, effort high)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultralight_nine_item_sweep", "label": "Nine-item all-concern sweep", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultralight.md", "source_location": "lines 59-91, 106-115", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One reviewer covers, in fixed order and without reordering or stopping early: requirements, correctness, error paths (given their own item rather than folded into correctness), separation of concerns (explicitly not to be compressed), placement, standards, security, tests, and surplus. The risk is not capacity \u2014 eligibility rules keep anything substantial away \u2014 it is attention drift, and the per-item log verdict for all nine items is the only evidence the lead has that the sweep happened rather than stopping at item three. A reviewer that reports it could not cover an item causes the lead to escalate, which is the correct outcome and not a failure."}, {"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultralight_wrong_loop_signal", "label": "Authz or untrusted input found here means the change is in the wrong loop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultralight.md", "source_location": "lines 84-86", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ultralight loop's eligibility rules should have kept authorization and untrusted input away entirely; finding either is evidence the routing decision was wrong, so the reviewer must say so prominently rather than simply reviewing it."}, {"id": "user__claude_skills_d